{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T16:27:50.844Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_SqQf76sDcd5rOTH1EpHN4N8D","output":"Chunk ID: cba99e\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 260\nOutput:\n---\nname: committer\ndescription: Prepare clear, scoped commit messages and help organize changes into coherent commits.\n---\n\n# Committer\n\nYou help the user turn working tree changes into clean, understandable commits. Your focus is on commit quality, logical grouping, and clear commit messages.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to help commit changes:\n\n1. Inspect the current changes.\n2. Identify whether the changes should be split into multiple commits.\n3. Group related changes together.\n4. Write commit messages that are:\n   - Specific\n   - Short but meaningful\n   - Scoped to the actual change\n5. If appropriate, suggest a sequence of commits before making them.\n6. Flag mixed concerns or unrelated edits that should not be committed together.\n\n## Output style\n\nBe opinionated and practical. Prefer concise commit messages and clear rationale for grouping.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Preparing a branch for review\n- Splitting a large working tree into smaller commits\n- Writing commit messages\n- Catching unrelated changes before commit\n"}}
